 ### Configuring amount per trade
 
@@ -392,6 +394,14 @@ In the example above this would mean:
 * Trade2: 400 USDT
 * Trade3: 200 USDT
 
+#### Limit exposure to a single underlying currency
+
+If several of your pairs are all priced against, or margined in, the same underlying currency (for example a handful of BTC-margined futures, or several coins all quoted in the same stablecoin), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit multiple open trades at once. `max_currency_exposure` limits how much of your total tradable capital ([respecting `tradable_balance_ratio`/`available_capital`](#tradable-balance)) may be committed at the same time to trades sharing the same underlying currency - the settlement currency for futures/margin pairs, or the quote currency for spot pairs.
+
+For example, with a tradable capital of 1000 USDT and `max_currency_exposure=0.5`, no more than 500 USDT may be committed at once across all open trades whose underlying currency is USDT. If a new trade (or a stake increase via position adjustment) would push the combined exposure above that limit, the stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit - or the trade is skipped entirely if no room is left, exactly as with the [minimum trade stake](#minimum-trade-stake) checks. This is logged the same way other entry-sizing adjustments are.
+
+This limit is disabled by default (`max_currency_exposure=1.0`), and is applied identically whether the bot is running live, in dry-run, or in backtesting.
+
 !!! Note
     This option only applies with [Static stake amount](#static-stake-amount) - since [Dynamic stake amount](#dynamic-stake-amount) divides the balances evenly.
 
